-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Renegade
  Publisher   Imagine, 1987
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Renegade (1987)(Imagine)(128K).z80
  MD5         9432bbad61d76f7e2a6e1a079c0f363a

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The fighters, bikers and gang members in fuller colour with more
              detail. Source: Enhanced colours from the MVV package's older
              Spec256 conversion, painter not established.

  Changes     1.1: the game keeps its own CPU speed after each sprite update
              instead of being set back to 3.5 MHz; works on NextZXOS v2.10
              (System/Next 26.11).

  Note        Known issues: none found in testing; pace in JNext -2.1 to +1.6%
              against the original over 600 game updates in 3 runs, default
              and Enhanced alike (the runs drift apart, so scenes are not
              compared like for like). Missing: the music was not listened to
              in testing; the cheats are the archive's 128K POKEs and have not
              been played; not yet checked: joysticks and the ending; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite time
   3  No death
   4  Easy fight, one-hit falls
   5  Start at level 2
   6  Start at level 3
   7  Start at level 4

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

